#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110216 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0cd1bb61-2770-5096-83d6-d1e4a7189e9a" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing \"Or Equal To\" Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "4b19b389-7d0e-525b-b37f-787e53f5e3b2" :question/math-academy-id "e-1056" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/bdb5279236cdc7671efa0f309b0a07d5ffc131f9d3c33a048f286fdef4588fcd.png)\n\nWhich system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y = 2x - 1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\leq 2x - 1.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y = -x+2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\geq -x + 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines our shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 2x-1 \\\\ y\\ge -x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110461 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbd52408-5f2f-58c9-9a88-bd992fe8752c" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Strict Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "ae48dbff-25c8-55a9-a9e0-fda0b3ecfd50" :question/math-academy-id "e-7959" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/c9209c8978b86043b5d57d4a357a480a0209914598a0d7f2a810539cc050c473.png)\n\nWhich system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=2x-3.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\gt 2x - 3.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y = x + 1.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\lt x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y>2x-3 \\\\ y<x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110462 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a258070e-5c3c-595e-81d6-3e0f9b9a5daf" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Mixed Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "4809beec-7c4e-5bd1-989d-1dc54d78d892" :question/math-academy-id "e-7960" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/69a4b7d160f9a3990034f7e9170cc20d90eba33bd87397f8436836fdd5520e84.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities represents the shaded region shown in the graph above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y = \\dfrac{1}{3}x+3.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\leq \\dfrac{1}{3}x+3.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y = x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\lt x+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\le \\frac{1}{3}x+3 \\\\ y<x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110463 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42525832-e186-538f-baf8-bb4418e9820b" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Inequalities Presented in Standard Form"}] :question/id #uuid "88a7aab5-813a-58e2-a695-8ee72dd4efb1" :question/math-academy-id "e-7964" :question/problem "What system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/e92ea6fc292a771333cc12b9554b58bd4ba5f358195982c5ac3fd6bd2a9d06ff.png)" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=1.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is \n\n$$\ny < 1.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $x - y = 2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny =x- 2.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\geq  x - 2,\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx-y \\leq 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y<1 \\\\ x-y\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285657 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0cd1bb61-2770-5096-83d6-d1e4a7189e9a" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing \"Or Equal To\" Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72443398-a4be-5ae0-95b9-bcb3fa2f8c88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285659} {:answer/id #uuid "21b59f67-c132-5893-a261-928896093713" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285660} {:answer/id #uuid "b1493575-3968-5c23-b3dc-de5e20d424f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y\\le -2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285661} {:answer/id #uuid "34684f91-5ec5-5189-a631-41707dc1b4fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<\\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y>-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285662} {:answer/id #uuid "9333e418-2366-5278-97fb-94ccc0a547df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y\\le -2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72443398-a4be-5ae0-95b9-bcb3fa2f8c88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285659} :answer-field/id #uuid "75867289-1a78-56c2-87a9-0e701061722a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285658}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72b9639e-3c97-59a1-8d1b-9bc526399985" :question/math-academy-id "q-109971" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/301b3a5f659be1efaa44d359d36acb055d45181b4d4e27b63f9fba7136e34867.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=-2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"gretaer than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbd52408-5f2f-58c9-9a88-bd992fe8752c" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Strict Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8dd9f321-aac6-5385-b9d5-0a3d0b097c9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<2x-3 \\\\ y<\\frac{1}{4}x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285666} {:answer/id #uuid "07279360-95e0-588c-9e13-a2e34220e803" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y>2x-3 \\\\ y<\\frac{1}{4}x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285667} {:answer/id #uuid "740a5315-bb25-52e1-9403-66c37261e04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y>2x-3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285668} {:answer/id #uuid "bd831b33-9a36-5740-9642-69ee05bdc350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<2x-3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285669} {:answer/id #uuid "dc4ea055-e745-52a4-a86a-ecac29bd009b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 2x-3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "740a5315-bb25-52e1-9403-66c37261e04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y>2x-3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285668} :answer-field/id #uuid "76544401-6782-55df-99e6-690e8a017826" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285665}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a72b44d-d61f-52de-a899-c22f95e1e7f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-109978" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/fbc2ecee3caa8572fe738affc7c607066ea985a1423ccef27d77f34e723c5877.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=2x-3.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>2x-3.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{4}x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>\\frac{1}{4}x+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y>2x-3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285671 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42525832-e186-538f-baf8-bb4418e9820b" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Inequalities Presented in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e20c320-1ad0-54fd-9512-fca352d508eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\le -8 \\\\ y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285673} {:answer/id #uuid "7520387a-23fa-57dd-a52f-8ec8d9a1cbc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y>-8 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{2}x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285674} {:answer/id #uuid "086537ea-0bb8-55cd-8b01-4ba255c377ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge -8 \\\\ y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285675} {:answer/id #uuid "a52f7431-2a01-5a64-9d67-f90694e6a8c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\le -8 \\\\ y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285676} {:answer/id #uuid "f74537c3-6e60-5002-ad5b-e9e4dd1021fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge -8 \\\\ y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f74537c3-6e60-5002-ad5b-e9e4dd1021fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge -8 \\\\ y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285677} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6d5d5a9-4693-5ade-aa80-35bfbbeb6fea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9a72356-7e05-5f10-b6ac-a2418c3b4fa6" :question/math-academy-id "q-110078" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/3905dacc3977857933a48ced329fc245b357f732aec520e67998efc0b5d7cdab.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $x+2y=-8.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x-4.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x-4,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+2y\\ge -8.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge -8 \\\\ y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285678 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42525832-e186-538f-baf8-bb4418e9820b" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Inequalities Presented in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37cf9a7b-f111-5151-b097-7ba5c6b36e1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge x+2 \\\\ 3x+2y>-6\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285680} {:answer/id #uuid "aafac6bf-fa64-5f67-b055-838d1a2dd82b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<x+2 \\\\ 3x+2y\\ge -6\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285681} {:answer/id #uuid "2c14bdfa-7862-5fff-ae20-ff46292f261b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y>x+2 \\\\ 3x+2y\\ge -6\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285682} {:answer/id #uuid "bb434c57-92d9-5052-9e27-6c98ffe0aa7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<x+2 \\\\ 3x+2y\\le -6\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285683} {:answer/id #uuid "4a5c86ba-7ef1-5631-be73-3b243dac1485" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ 3x+2y>-6\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb434c57-92d9-5052-9e27-6c98ffe0aa7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<x+2 \\\\ 3x+2y\\le -6\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285683} :answer-field/id #uuid "682e4370-544d-5089-aa88-668ba19ee4b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285679}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2dff6eda-c649-5ce9-b940-098322fd6bdf" :question/math-academy-id "q-110093" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/f03b04087cde111d9db2b9e499a0d700105b7150496cc6c117c0f2e2b05e74c2.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $3x+2y=-6.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{3}{2}x-3.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le -\\frac{3}{2}x-3,\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n3x+2y\\le -6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y<x+2 \\\\ 3x+2y\\le -6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0cd1bb61-2770-5096-83d6-d1e4a7189e9a" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing \"Or Equal To\" Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "318c5bfa-d37b-5834-8eed-cbc34df40462" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/a08b02234e684a2a99394f8614eb8b685fb7d7053ce7670a105e175d8a68d987.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285687} {:answer/id #uuid "9854d1e8-c4fd-5059-a9b0-fcf4362f2928" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/7f6c2420a2d0b