 Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, the line itself is included in the solution, so the line is solid.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* or equal to those on the line, so we shade *above* the line.\n\nTo graph the second inequality $y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x.$ \n\n- Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, the line itself is included in the solution, so the line is solid.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* or equal to those on the line, so we shade *below* the line.\n\nThe intersection of the solutions is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/6190eb782fb731535c261e85e11fa5e20b3894c3602ed94a834ba5b2dd752135.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a258070e-5c3c-595e-81d6-3e0f9b9a5daf" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Mixed Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb8e23df-0c3a-58af-85a5-64af5589138a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/787f7be05501971bb09a94d3c821a80e3e92339ade84331ff671aa1d26740762.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285694} {:answer/id #uuid "6376b727-922a-5d2a-9eb8-bc04356730f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/32119e434937cea1c3179c7828f1bdda62ddee28ba6ce77f49ca0307b7f541f3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285695} {:answer/id #uuid "faab36e1-2811-5465-8870-d73a099100b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/15608503fc9aa3ffe20cd649cf2d0adab657a09961811c206a7bce16a34c9c2f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 1759