the line itself is *not* included in the solution, so the line is dashed.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than*  those on the line, so we shade *above* the line.\n\nThe intersection of the solutions is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/15608503fc9aa3ffe20cd649cf2d0adab657a09961811c206a7bce16a34c9c2f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbd52408-5f2f-58c9-9a88-bd992fe8752c" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Strict Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c50f0ed-6e97-55bc-a45f-dfab2238cd23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/9a77273989d5077d2c711f4f5c67eba26f3f2b6d8494933a5b573959b56ae0c2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285701} {:answer/id #uuid "4b156fbb-4362-5999-9b32-039ab74959c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/701181ee3a695238f6872ae289174360cdd47e8580721a39e7aaeea49be97978.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285702} {:answer/id #uuid "e2a2f78d-9060-52c0-9a4d-084eab938e05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/78b1215deb9c3990c7636a619f1ed459731cc8c5577d6840900f8212c220d5f4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285703} {:answer/id #uuid "3b982c62-fe79-50b9-93ec-be90aba65356" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/9d367b12f56fde031940dc3194f8300eb4d5e40b9ec793c7d35a5808f5d14996.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285704} {:answer/id #uuid "ca967359-2366-5d08-b596-dd9e876e49cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/95c4447f15114c76d2c2a108b5df1b4587142dc366ac3f7151dac69cf4597f6d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285705}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b982c62-fe79-50b9-93ec-be90aba65356" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/9d367b12f56fde031940dc3194f8300eb4d5e40b9ec793c7d35a5808f5d14996.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285704} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2a294eb-c782-5ce2-9b49-b44184ec183b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ff007862-3cae-526c-9488-26e508257290" :question/math-academy-id "q-25199" :question/problem "Which of the diagrams shows the solution of the following system?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y>x+2 \\\\ y<2x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To graph the first inequality $y>x+2,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=x+2.$\n\n- Since we have a strict inequality, the line itself is *not* included in the solution, so the line is dashed.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* those on the line, so we shade *above* the line.\n\nTo graph the second inequality $y<2x-2,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=2x-2.$\n\n- Since we have a strict inequality, the line itself is *not* included in the solution, so the line is dashed.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* those on the line, so we shade *below* the line.\n\nThe intersection of the solutions is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/9d367b12f56fde031940dc3194f8300eb4d5e40b9ec793c7d35a5808f5d14996.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285706 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a258070e-5c3c-595e-81d6-3e0f9b9a5daf" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Mixed Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19cea25a-af7f-57a0-9173-d01da0144bff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y>-x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285708} {:answer/id #uuid "d496967f-a712-554a-bdd0-89fc29c1a918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285709} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf6fc34-9053-50eb-8ed7-fa2f1334e1ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y>x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285710} {:answer/id #uuid "a869f11f-df5f-5908-bd57-581ddc0ed096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge x+2 \\\\ y<-x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285711} {:answer/id #uuid "ebd720e1-ee7b-5bec-9a68-26c67903bf39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y<-x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbf6fc34-9053-50eb-8ed7-fa2f1334e1ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y>x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285710} :answer-field/id #uuid "37b67032-2819-5fb7-a3c9-b918ce7b5ac2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5cb8229e-2a6a-582b-a6c3-627b88cf6816" :question/math-academy-id "q-29384" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/a740aafbb9f74e2681506d3027f848fa92e7eea2bac3e08ccaf3fc7e0acf8fa1.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown in the graph above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=-x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y>x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285713 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a258070e-5c3c-595e-81d6-3e0f9b9a5daf" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Mixed Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c49b7f8-1bda-51fd-9ee5-e6e6eac02d44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/a34a6e8b90dc1efecb62a3312cf67d2e8f65d96ece1b4f11eb0e202e391f9f6b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285715} {:answer/id #uuid "27e2dd8c-8a18-552b-ae07-e2eb7313d1d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/16a0fc9276e3fb8b2b15db8562e75479c80731081c12457397ee7479c527c2e0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285716} {:answer/id #uuid "b543a154-8458-54dc-9327-3757a0f1d20a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/8dad9f3b7c5deaddcc35ee9f17f0e9ee891869f6f3aa35c83f1a50152e9cf8da.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285717} {:answer/id #uuid "fa0b7ca9-31ec-51cc-87d4-8bb429474703" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/d2ce8abd902ce4025c6d3477558fbe94c7f07a3c3a2afb2c6853e5c914ac4a0d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285718} {:answer/id #uuid "8ce849cf-a06b-57c7-ad3a-0857e5f78200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/e949882745de4727e3f611b8f958b64ed6fc08c0097508970501a16f68374cf2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ce849cf-a06b-57c7-ad3a-0857e5f78200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/e949882745de4727e3f611b8f958b64ed6fc08c0097508970501a16f68374cf2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285719} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fdb883c-f5b1-595c-8e04-f03099349f41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285714}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cf2fb8b9-9f5b-5331-bd50-34adc1652a8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-29393" :question/problem "Which of the diagrams shows the solution of the following system?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y<2 \\\\ y\\ge -2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To graph the first inequality $y<2,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=2.$\n\n- Since we have a strict inequality, the line itself is *not* included in the solution, so the line is dashed.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* those on the line, so we shade *below* the line.\n\nTo graph the second inequality $y\\ge -2,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=-2.$\n\n- Since we have a \"or equal to\" inequality, the line itself is included in the solution, so the line is solid.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* or equal to those on the line, so we shade *above* the line.\n\nThe intersection of the solutions is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/e949882745de4727e3f611b8f958b64ed6fc08c0097508970501a16f68374cf2.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285720 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0cd1bb61-2770-5096-83d6-d1e4a7189e9a" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing \"Or Equal To\" Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdab1908-5c6c-5fdf-afe6-7b1157532d1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285722} {:answer/id #uuid "e0a516b0-48a5-5718-b624-504caa676dd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\le 2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285723} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc0951f-f08e-5a75-8f9d-dd0658d8d8b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y<2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285724} {:answer/id #uuid "f5145e93-9caa-518c-a4e1-935044117bd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 3x+1 \\\\ y\\le 2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285725} {:answer/id #uuid "4412bfed-5686-5f2a-957f-c04ea717913a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdab1908-5c6c-5fdf-afe6-7b1157532d1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285722} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5042dfe-9d9b-51ee-8f12-166de67e5b6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9187138f-ae2f-5a56-952a-6135b67724bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-52413" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/75a7f3bfae55a97fbc0c05e2e0356d21de6ceabcc82ac3e1c965838a636f5ecc.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=3x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 3x+1.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285727 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbd52408-5f2f-58c9-9a88-bd992fe8752c" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Strict Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8040a30-2003-5cd4-8b61-d69ca60af048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<2x+6 \\\\ y>5\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285729} {:answer/id #uuid "fc5f5c4d-b85e-56ec-8c3f-e2760e992a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<2x+6 \\\\ y<5\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285730} {:answer/id #uuid "44bbaa99-5340-556c-a614-65a069ef2e09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 2x+6 \\\\ y\\le 5\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285731} {:answer/id #uuid "51e83183-a051-5ccc-8110-772ba24eacb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y>2x+6 \\\\ y<5\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285732} {:answer/id #uuid "fb5617ac-8f4a-5cc1-823a-c2bd3f057f81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y>2x+6 \\\\ y>5\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc5f5c4d-b85e-56ec-8c3f-e2760e992a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<2x+6 \\\\ y<5\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285730} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c8e7962-af4e-5cf4-b5f0-e0e9335ce419" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d48a81ca-ca4e-5354-bd11-f73315ba7d7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-52461" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/ba01cf5268f2bd62835c925a5eb793c0d98663948899c9e9aba2eeacd37ff30a.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=2x+6.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<2x+6.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=5.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y<2x+6 \\\\ y<5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285734 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbd52408-5f2f-58c9-9a88-bd992fe8752c" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Strict Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "274c16cd-6f41-5e8b-bb60-606e0e9cc044" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y>3x+2 \\\\ y>1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285736} {:answer/id #uuid "db04390a-0581-5b57-b07d-b2d1c0753ca4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 3x+2 \\\\ y\\le 1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285737} {:answer/id #uuid "feebae6c-c15c-5a5a-b3d8-ded1f5aa7bdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<3x+2 \\\\ y>1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285738} {:answer/id #uuid "780d0cfe-3805-5599-83b6-80a800797f5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<3x+2 \\\\ y<1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285739} {:answer/id #uuid "6c59c404-815b-52a2-b571-ce5bc463f98a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y>3x+2 \\\\ y<1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285740}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "780d0cfe-3805-5599-83b6-80a800797f5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<3x+2 \\\\ y<1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285739} :answer-field/id #uuid "34a0fdf8-d284-5075-a8e3-dcb826005a89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d7407375-6d86-5c5a-9b91-fed1c63e1fe6" :question/math-academy-id "q-52462" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/b296ca9f6ffcb6feca8169b0eb02ced3c65f4ea59c0f331568292302dea8fea9.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=3x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<3x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=1.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y<3x+2 \\\\ y<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285741 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42525832-e186-538f-baf8-bb4418e9820b" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Inequalities Presented in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66a652be-4ace-51bb-9d9a-d7be8d4af41b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\le 2 \\\\ y\\le 2x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285743} {:answer/id #uuid "ac94eeb5-f671-5969-9c0b-4b4255577d9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge 2 \\\\ y\\le 2x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285744} {:answer/id #uuid "adda46e0-af1c-5980-819d-c3c6a802b817" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y>2 \\\\ y>2x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285745} {:answer/id #uuid "a0731404-8e84-5f2b-91a5-386851fe33be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\le 2 \\\\ y\\ge 2x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285746} {:answer/id #uuid "9cd0a2d8-4950-57e7-8098-404e6b7e0350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge 2 \\\\ y\\ge 2x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac94eeb5-f671-5969-9c0b-4b4255577d9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge 2 \\\\ y\\le 2x+1\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285744} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f5ba861-bd3f-5bdc-8a99-8037a316c2c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285742}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ed9fe7c-113c-5500-8621-37e2099caf94" :question/math-academy-id "q-90053" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/4b3487492c235ddeaa46d6b64cc3cc908e02bacf061ab84474401c9d6e3ce634.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $x+2y=2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+1.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x+1,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+2y\\ge 2.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=2x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le 2x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge 2 \\\\ y\\le 2x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285748 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42525832-e186-538f-baf8-bb4418e9820b" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Inequalities Presented in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "547d549c-6d56-54bb-9657-9c82d479af6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+y<3 \\\\ y>2x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285750} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e2982e-43a7-549e-9480-0044d5ca0439" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+y\\le 3 \\\\ y\\ge 2x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285751} {:answer/id #uuid "37c6a689-8f90-5928-8072-e7561e4ca818" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y<2x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285752} {:answer/id #uuid "8a801817-1254-5bad-9d17-f31f91472ef0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+y<3 \\\\ y<2x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285753} {:answer/id #uuid "5be083a2-f802-59f7-9698-f87a8b4f972e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y>2x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5be083a2-f802-59f7-9698-f87a8b4f972e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y>2x\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285754} :answer-field/id #uuid "e328baeb-8594-5f4f-b976-26a3555769b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285749}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "262609c0-5557-5285-b43c-f82fdb8825a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-90054" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/b8c1d5902a76a68e5f8358d4c3668e1be184ec7241184df4ff1363d41995f3aa.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $x+y=3.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-x+3.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\"  inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>-x+3,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+y>3.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=2x.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict.  Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>2x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y>3 \\\\ y>2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111346 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42525832-e186-538f-baf8-bb4418e9820b" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Inequalities Presented in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a0e65a4-494b-574a-a747-6e72fdf12a2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y \\ge 2x; x - 4y < - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110172} {:answer/id #uuid "2559e0cf-8a05-526b-ae8c-e92045fb0ab2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y > 2x; x - 4y \\le - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110173} {:answer/id #uuid "281905c7-96bc-55c7-8e46-e301849e57ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y < 2x; x - 4y \\ge - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110174} {:answer/id #uuid "6547a7db-483a-51ea-9edd-c26e2945ec50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y < 2x; x - 4y \\le - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110175} {:answer/id #uuid "778c9ec6-64db-5f8f-93a3-24e78dee7551" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y > 2x; x - 4y \\ge - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "778c9ec6-64db-5f8f-93a3-24e78dee7551" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y > 2x; x - 4y \\ge - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110176} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7d0056c-dfbc-582e-a57b-a8a8b93ed7ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186110171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c3f4183-c4d9-5b11-be2e-1b8454dc99ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-90171" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/06519bbe714e1ad2e8b878e7c6a6026cbad7b846b06f16fbdd3c478c18f9db88.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=2x.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>2x.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $x-4y=-8.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{4}+2.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le \\frac{x}{4}+2,\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx-4y\\ge -8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y>2x \\\\ x-4y\\ge -8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285755 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0cd1bb61-2770-5096-83d6-d1e4a7189e9a" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing \"Or Equal To\" Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f19a9777-c2a4-5658-9bff-98696f2ba5bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/438928da5e9de5e9ba3d2abbe06b6f1f8b6b0598a0b82bec1f51824b9ef72a71.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285757} {:answer/id #uuid "0bae1111-86d3-54d6-87d0-675012c7d741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/27ba3ad2783e64a6b29d5ea488d63fc634d2a43ee01d6a77c4802da8bc06b641.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285758} {:answer/id #uuid "dc0f9116-614d-5b26-a981-10529174bea3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/197ae7933ece17a22bdf17c2397053541891a789892813599930de273496cd78.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285759} {:answer/id #uuid "d30bafdc-238e-5a70-91d3-a1a562192ce5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/e5428cead5e96d930e52a833942a1c4452c43f3e2f6ba7c6fc39758ee83e8d81.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285760} {:answer/id #uuid "b0f1eba5-95ff-5e37-ad58-4637afa26dda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/bb0ea125af03527a6e3111fc638f5fd9a4efaa39bc7b48a82e2efcfcfb0b696b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f19a9777-c2a4-5658-9bff-98696f2ba5bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/438928da5e9de5e9ba3d2abbe06b6f1f8b6b0598a0b82bec1f51824b9ef72a71.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285757} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cd88b33-8246-582c-82b1-14015bb25b1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285756}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "12b718de-1f28-5ec6-b73e-0c704e48e717" :question/math-academy-id "q-90174" :question/problem "Which of the diagrams shows the solution of the following system?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 2x \\\\ y\\le -2x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To graph the first inequality $y\\le 2x,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=2x.$\n\n- Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, the line itself is included in the solution, so the line is solid.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* or equal to those on the line, so we shade *below* the line.\n\nTo graph the second inequality $y\\le -2x,$ we draw the corresponding straight line $y=-2x.$ \n\n- Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, the line itself is included in the solution, so the line is solid.\n\n- The inequality refers to the $y$-values that are *less than* or equal to those on the line, so we shade *below* the line.\n\nThe intersection of the solutions is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/438928da5e9de5e9ba3d2abbe06b6f1f8b6b0598a0b82bec1f51824b9ef72a71.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285762 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0cd1bb61-2770-5096-83d6-d1e4a7189e9a" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing \"Or Equal To\" Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e3b7ac0-f067-5e58-ac08-9b001e0733da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ y\\ge 2x+3\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285764} {:answer/id #uuid "ffff49c6-2842-503d-9c4a-be6bbb4a33e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y>\\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ y<2x+3\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285765} {:answer/id #uuid "f47499b3-cdde-5078-a255-0fbbfa5226cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<\\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ y\\ge 2x+3\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285766} {:answer/id #uuid "63549342-1232-566b-a443-dde0c6de1677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ y\\le 2x+3\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285767} {:answer/id #uuid "cdca9b88-a821-57f6-b271-9a266e0ad00f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ y\\le 2x+3\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdca9b88-a821-57f6-b271-9a266e0ad00f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ y\\le 2x+3\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285768} :answer-field/id #uuid "b218b3ae-ef7b-5cc5-a9e3-f51be7a603dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285763}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "677e7c64-35d2-5c41-9614-74f7425157cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-90319" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/387709ca72b5591528b5f5ac95886f0dab331ef2cb67955803e7a252cecef966.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=2x+3.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le 2x+3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines our shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge \\frac{1}{2}x \\\\ y\\le 2x+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285769 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fbd52408-5f2f-58c9-9a88-bd992fe8752c" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Strict Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48aba70c-269f-5009-8233-110eb521fbf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285771} {:answer/id #uuid "cc6ea2e8-4c6f-52cf-99bc-09704c5fab46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285772} {:answer/id #uuid "fd714f62-ecf4-59ed-aaf4-8bbec0a70238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y>4x+3 \\\\ y\\ge \\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285773} {:answer/id #uuid "13fef3c6-28a0-526a-8dc2-fb5af84be015" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y>4x+3 \\\\ y<\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285774} {:answer/id #uuid "1b3e0d73-d4d7-5df9-a67a-795a1394939d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y>4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc6ea2e8-4c6f-52cf-99bc-09704c5fab46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285772} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e71ab45-8c5f-5c27-935a-6cd13b0fe292" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66b0d8c5-2487-53cc-b840-b06edcc12d56" :question/math-academy-id "q-90323" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/e863789ff989ee1cb3d3fe6c22fe0d4daa1dac76d6fbfbebdad801006ca4c969.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=4x+3.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<4x+3.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{4}x-2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>\\frac{1}{4}x-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y<4x+3 \\\\ y>\\frac{1}{4}x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285776 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a258070e-5c3c-595e-81d6-3e0f9b9a5daf" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Mixed Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3b39a47-697a-5da9-8de0-2530f93c0d2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285778} {:answer/id #uuid "72dc68f1-daeb-5c0b-9818-63741267f8d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y>x+2 \\\\ y\\le -x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285779} {:answer/id #uuid "a13e5e1e-f18d-5d74-bbca-6a8c7c47a883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y>-x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285780} {:answer/id #uuid "6275a9e7-3fc1-5649-8d1d-21bef56c3175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge x+2 \\\\ y<-x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285781} {:answer/id #uuid "67e7c149-2f84-53ae-b7fe-0eaec519969a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<x+2 \\\\ y\\ge -x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285782}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a13e5e1e-f18d-5d74-bbca-6a8c7c47a883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y>-x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285780} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab9fd4aa-2c71-5747-8648-7cf2a5f1176d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285777}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3e5e2c49-2afd-5324-972b-43974f8bfdd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-90327" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/762e53967ddb3ccddfa1c9b7a2aa303d66fc1b761c9be8f409c0b91ecb0201de.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities represents the shaded region shown in the graph above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=x+2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le x+2.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=-x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny>-x+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\le x+2 \\\\ y>-x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285783 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a258070e-5c3c-595e-81d6-3e0f9b9a5daf" :knowledge-point/title "Working With Systems Containing Mixed Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb10c58d-4b24-5129-8eb1-12791746fefb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 2x-4 \\\\ y<-\\frac{1}{2}x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285785} {:answer/id #uuid "2f63c477-a368-5f4b-b034-50f3310e67c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 2x-4 \\\\ y>-\\frac{1}{2}x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285786} {:answer/id #uuid "3d6bc9bf-c434-5a48-bca6-aa38d40a742b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y<2x-4 \\\\ y\\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285787} {:answer/id #uuid "fd676101-d7a0-5145-854d-76d65865f8f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 2x-4 \\\\ y>-\\frac{1}{2}x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285788} {:answer/id #uuid "674b707d-14f9-5b22-a542-d92f5d2e63f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y>2x-4 \\\\ y\\le -\\frac{1}{2}x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb10c58d-4b24-5129-8eb1-12791746fefb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 2x-4 \\\\ y<-\\frac{1}{2}x+2\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285785} :answer-field/id #uuid "6132937b-f0b2-524d-b808-d0037b584485" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6dc6793e-fa65-56d2-ab8b-152fb90933bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-90328" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/79222482da6f597532f514fe67facb3e9eefddbb7c1bf491dd3eac480e0886e2.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities represents the shaded region shown in the graph above?" :question/worked-solution "Consider the line $y=2x-4.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 2x-4.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x+2.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<-\\frac{1}{2}x+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 2x-4 \\\\ y<-\\frac{1}{2}x+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
